{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"content_hash":"6192bf8302a20700d883f8e27bea46437d6551e0edf9af2f3e111980a50fd0aa","digest":{"component_or_area":"Operation-scoped configuration and provider-auth composition","key_entities":["OperationSnapshot","RP-01","RP-04","ADR 0098","PydanticAIRunner","ProviderSession","GitRuntime","LLMRuntime","BridgeRuntime","op-cert","REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH","REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY","REBAR_ROOT","check_config_reads.py","Langfuse","OTLP","SecretStr","SecretBytes","S1 cotton-only-cuckoo","S2 titanium-chocolatey-kakapo","S3 talismanic-profitable-isopod","S4 distended-bipartisan-arkshell","S5 typical-neutral-waterbug","S6 ultrashort-immoderate-seriema","S7 junior-lepidolite-boa"],"problem_keywords":["configuration resolution","provider authentication composition","credential management","operation scoping","ambient state","runtime bindings"],"propositions":["Configuration resolution must follow a single immutable precedence order (explicit operation input > environment > project config > user config > schema default) without rereading ambient state mid-operation","Provider authentication (LLM, Git, bridge, MCP, review-bot, observability, op-cert) must be composed consistently with provider-native credential lifecycles and injected only through approved seams (e.g., PydanticAIRunner ProviderSession for LLM)","Static credentials must be represented as provider-specific non-serializable carriers (SecretStr/SecretBytes) and revealed only in sending adapters, never persisted in snapshots, logs, exceptions, or global environment","Op-cert must accept exactly one of REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH or REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY, validate at startup, store in process-owned 0700/0600 storage, and rotate only on restart—with no runtime SSM/boto3 retrieval","Same-capability children inherit ambient environment for compatibility; owning children receive only their adapter overlay; unrelated siblings lose exact secret names declared by other Rebar adapters","An AST ownership gate must derive config/credential names from authoritative registries, reject unauthorized reads/reloads/defaults, permit only exact path/symbol+rationale exceptions, and reach zero legacy exceptions at cutover"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787565799144821001,"uuid":"bcf2a95b-6fbb-4c77-9ba5-126d2d5b3aa5"}